    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0546" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg526"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795B.5/8–150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Korea </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-08-04T14:00:00-04:00">August 4, 1950—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. Reurtel 98<anchor n="1" xml:id="d395-f1"/> Dept understands from Dept Defense
                    that emergency auth given Gen MacArthur immed fol outbreak hostilities
                    permitting him, as operational expedient, fulfill, without limitation, all
                    KMAG’s requests for material on behalf ROK. It further understood MacArthur
                    utilizing this auth to meet current requirements Korean forces.</p>
                <p>For your further info Dept informing NSC its opinion that NSC 8/2<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d395-f2"/> which imposed limitation of 65,000 troops, now
                    obsolete.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
